  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tSelf Assessment \n\t\tSelf Assessment Help Guide\n\n### SA100 Tax Calculations\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 11 Feb, 2021 at  5:10 PM\n\n### This section of the SA100 Return gives you five options to navigate through:\n\n - \n### Self-Assessment (this is where the system calculates tax automatically based on your entries)\n\n - \n### Underpaid tax and other Debts \n\n - \n### Payments on Account   \n\n - \n### Blind person’s surplus account and Married Couple’s Surplus Account   \n\n - \n### Adjustments to Tax Due\n\n### \n\n### \n\n### \n\n### \n\nClick here to watch how to manually enter Payment on Accounts (PoA)\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
